# Copy this to `denylist.local` (untracked) and add your private terms.
# One term/regex per line; blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
# Blocked IN ADDITION to the hook's built-in generic patterns (home paths, emails),
# so no identifying info ever lives in the tracked repo.
#
# Or set an env var instead of this file:
#   export CLAUDE_CONFIG_DENYLIST="term1|term2"
#
# Examples (replace with your own):
#   my-employer-name
#   my-client-codename
